Z||000006||batboy||08-15-99||09:48 AM||||Yippee! Oh boy! I can't wait to start hearing about these turbo upgrades. At least three or four Forum regulars either have turbos or planning to install them. I think if the costs are low enough and adapting it to fit is not too hard, this is a great way to increase power.<p>It would be cool to have dyno tests and 1/4 mile times for before and after on a couple different cars. I'd be willing to post the results and a brief description on my website if need be.<p>The intercoolers are much easier on the turbo bearings, but remember this: turbos just require a lot of bearing maintainance, especially if you use them often.<p>Don't turbos like low compression? Like 8:1 and 8.5:1 ratios? Will it work ok with the stock V6 ratio? Also, I'd use a set of good forged pistons (if you can find them) or at least hypereutectics, assuming this is a major rebuild.
